   "subject": "RxODE error",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve made a testing RxODE shiny app which runs fine on my own computer. It just won&#39;t run on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_fn3tNqvlAzar6aTTgMQi\">shinyapps.io</a> online though and I keep seeing this error message:</div><div><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\">ERROR: Error sourcing /srv/connect/apps/myapp/app.R</pre></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m suspecting it&#39;s because the package needs to send the code to a temporary folder on the local computer with a compiler - it requires Rtools on the local computer to run - and dynamically load that back to R. In fact, the app won&#39;t run properly if the temporary folder is not specified. Is there a way we can run this kind of app on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701944000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2_fn3tNqvlAzar6aTTgMQi\">shinyapps.io</a>? </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks so you for your help. </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Zuays-oCAQAJ",
