    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div><blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hello,</p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;ve made a testing RxODE shiny app which runs fine on my own computer. It just won&#39;t run on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701949000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0MK6Lh4_HtA0QaK_j7ePM8\">shinyapps.io</a> online though and I keep seeing this error message:</p></div><div><pre style=\"word-wrap:break-word;white-space:pre-wrap\"><span style=\"color:black\">ERROR: Error sourcing /srv/connect/apps/myapp/app.R</span></pre></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I&#39;m suspecting it&#39;s because the package needs to send the code to a temporary folder on the local computer with a compiler - it requires Rtools on the local computer to run - and dynamically load that back to R. In fact, the app won&#39;t run properly if the temporary folder is not specified. Is there a way we can run this kind of app on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701949000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0MK6Lh4_HtA0QaK_j7ePM8\">shinyapps.io</a>? </p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"> </p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks so you for your help. </p></div></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
