   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>I don&#39;t have lines calling readLines in my app.R script, so I suspect that&#39;s the functions in the RxODE package calling it?</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;m new to the packages, but if it is of any help, the package developer advised me:</div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">&quot;As to the ShinyApp question, it really depends on the nature\r\nof your web server. For instance, if you web server is on linux, you\r\ncannot just copy the shinyapp generated from windows. You&#39;ll have to\r\nre-generate a shinyapp with RxODE on the native web server &amp; load it per\r\nyour web server configuration. You may have to consult your web master\r\nhow to get this step.&quot;<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><br></div><div>The following app.R script runs fine locally on my Windows computer with Rtools installed, but won&#39;t run properly on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701950000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1wApdI4swTpX4ITSew4c6h\">shinyapps.io</a> with this error message: </div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);white-space:pre-wrap\">&quot;ERROR: Error sourcing /srv/connect/apps/myapp/app.R&quot;</span></div><div><br></div><div><div><div>#Load packages</div><div>library(shiny)</div><div>library(RxODE)</div><div>#Model</div><div>ode &lt;- &quot;</div><div>  Cp = B/Vc;</div><div>  K10 = Cl/Vc;</div><div>  d/dt(A) = -Ka*A;</div><div>  d/dt(B) =  Ka*A -K10*B;</div><div>&quot;</div><div>tmp &lt;- tempfile()</div><div>m1 &lt;- RxODE(model=ode, modName=&quot;m1&quot;, wd=tmp)</div><div>inits &lt;- c(A=0,B=0,C=0)</div><div>tha = c(Ka = 2.39,Cl = 0.315,Vc = 0.516)<br></div><div>#UI</div><div>ui &lt;- fixedPage(</div><div>    sidebarLayout(</div><div>      sidebarPanel(</div><div>        sliderInput(&quot;DOSE&quot;,&quot;Dose (mg):&quot;,min = 0, max = 10, value = 5, step = 1)),</div><div>      mainPanel(plotOutput(&quot;plot1&quot;))</div><div>    )</div><div>)</div><div>#Server</div><div>server &lt;-(function(input, output){</div><div>  Dose = reactive({input$DOSE})</div><div>  sim &lt;- reactive({<br></div><div>    dose &lt;- Dose()</div><div>    ev &lt;- eventTable(amount.units=&quot;µg&quot;, time.units=&quot;hours&quot;)</div><div>    ev$add.sampling(seq(0,24,0.5))</div><div>    ev$add.dosing(dose=d,<a href=\"http://dosing.to\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dosing.to&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360701950000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2tQaB9Cus0PGYlH0zIcW17\">dosing.to</a>=1,nbr.doses=1,dosing.interval=24)</div><div>    sim &lt;- m1$solve(tha,ev,inits)})</div><div>  output$plot1 &lt;- renderPlot({</div><div>    x &lt;- sim()</div><div>    plot(x[,&quot;time&quot;],x[,&quot;Cp&quot;],type=&quot;l&quot;,xlab=&quot;Time&quot;,ylab=&quot;Conc&quot;)})</div><div>})</div></div><div><br></div></div><div>Thanks!</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><br>On Monday, August 14, 2017 at 2:37:31 PM UTC+2, Joshua Spiewak wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Could you either share the lines from app.R that are calling readLines, or the entire app.R so we can take a look?<br><br></div></blockquote></div>"
